D. Phase 1: Adapter Library Reuse
The first phase fits the new task with the library alone, before any new capacity is added. All new adapters are disabled, so that Eq. (1) reduces to a linear combination of past adapters, and onlyc (t) is trained under the backbone’s imitation lossL im, stopping when the loss plateaus. The remaining error indicates what the library alone cannot express, and the later phases add new adapters to cover it.
