d under the protocol and metrics above. All experiments run on a single NVIDIA A100 (80 GB) GPU per task stream.
B. Main Results
Table I shows the results on the four LIBERO suites. SARAM achieves the highest SRfinal and AUC on all four suites and the lowest NBT on three of them, while maintaining competitive FWT. Compared with adapter-based approaches, SARAM provides substantially stronger retention across the evaluated suites. SARAM also outperforms ER in AUC across all suites without retaining past demonstrations. SHARE performs poorly across all suites, suggesting that a single shared adapter is insufficient in this setting. Overall, these results show that the proposed approach maintains both task acquisition and retention across the evaluated task streams.


